# Profiled point-to-point platform move (trajectory_node, TRAJECTORY mode only).
# Every request is validated through the single feasibility gate before any motion;
# an infeasible request is rejected loudly (accepted=false) and never silently
# dropped.

geometry_msgs/Pose pose      # Target pose. Position in mm, z STOW-relative (170 = ACTIVE).
                             # Orientation as a quaternion (converted to a rotvec internally).
float64 duration_s           # Requested move duration (s). 0 => use the minimal feasible duration.
---
bool accepted                # True iff the move was planned and installed.
string code                  # Feasibility code: OK / UNREACHABLE / WORKSPACE / LIMIT_VEL /
                             # LIMIT_ACC / LIMIT_JERK / TOO_FAST / STEP_BOUND / WRONG_MODE / STALE_STATE.
string message               # Human-readable detail (populated on both accept and reject).
float64 planned_duration_s   # The duration actually used (>= duration_s; the stretched/minimal value).
float64 min_duration_s       # Minimal feasible duration for this move at the current limits
                             # (populated on a TOO_FAST rejection so the caller can retry achievably).
